#: ../chapter11.rst:3
msgid "Tenant Administrator"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter11.rst:5
msgid "Please reference the `Admin Guide`__ for full documentation of the tenant administration. Here we will go over several commonly touched areas for tenant administrators."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter11.rst:10
msgid "After you enter the \"management console\", you will be in the tenant manager. You can access the tenant by clicking on the desired tenant from the options."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter11.rst:15
msgid "Under Management Console, an admin can configure storage, monitor shared objects, create and manage team folders, manage users, configure granular group policies, add new tenant administrators, look at different reports, and under advanced configure AD etc."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter11.rst:17
msgid "After you click a tenant, you will be in the tenant dashboard. You can click through to different managers. You can manage users **(1)** and folders **(2)**. If you are using an Active Directory for importing users and permissions you can connect to your Active Directory by clicking the \"Configure Now\" **(3)**."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter11.rst:22
msgid "MANAGE USERS AND FILES"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter11.rst:27
msgid "User Manager"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter11.rst:29
msgid "You can access the user manager by clicking one of these items in the Tenant Dashboard."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter11.rst:34
msgid "ACCESSING THE USER MANAGER"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter11.rst:38
msgid "Active Directory - LDAP"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter11.rst:40
msgid "When you \"Create or Migrate User\" **(1)** in user manager, there are some options for adding new users. Click \"Active Directory\" **(2)**, you can add your local AD settings. Select \"Enable Active Directory Integration\" **(3)**."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter11.rst:45
msgid "CONNECTING TO ACTIVE DIRECTORY (AD)"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter11.rst:47
msgid "This gives you access to all the settings fields and the Advanced Settings Tab **(4)**. Once you have filled in the settings with an Administrator User account from your Active Directory, click **APPLY** to accept your changes."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter11.rst:51
msgid "Add Users"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter11.rst:53
msgid "You can add users from within the User Manager by clicking the \"Create or Migrate User\" button to open the **\"Options for Adding New Users\"** panel. In that panel you have several options: add a Native User, Batch Create Users, import Active Directory users and permissions, and if you have Server Agents actively connected, you will also see those servers listed here as well."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter11.rst:58
msgid "ADDING USERS"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter11.rst:60
msgid "**Native User**"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter11.rst:62
msgid "Native user refers to |prodname| user that is not related to any Active Directory."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter11.rst:65
msgid "**Batch create users**"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter11.rst:67
msgid "These are native users in a comma separated file that can be paste into a text area so the users can be batch created."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter11.rst:70
msgid "**Active Directory**"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter11.rst:72
msgid "Active Directory means users from Local Area Network (LAN) that is in the same network as the |prodname| server."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter11.rst:75
msgid "**Server-Agent-Name**"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter11.rst:77
msgid "If you already have the \"Server Agent\" installed and the server agent is actively connected to |prodname|, you will also see the server agents listed by name in the Add User page."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter11.rst:83
msgid "Native Users"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter11.rst:85
msgid "When a new user is created, the administrator will specify the amount of cloud storage that the new user is allowed to use. The email address will send a welcome email to the new user and will serve as his/her username."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter11.rst:90
msgid "ADDING A NATIVE USER"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter11.rst:94
msgid "When quota is left as zero, it means no limitation until the tenant quota limit is hit."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter11.rst:97
msgid "Active Directory Users from LDAP"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter11.rst:99
msgid "If the Active Directory (LDAP) is not already configured, you will need to configure it first. You can from \"Settings\" > \"Active Directory\", or \"Create or Migrate User\" > \"Active Directory\" to access the settings."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter11.rst:104
msgid "CONFIGURE YOUR ACTIVE DIRECTORY SETTINGS"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter11.rst:106
msgid "If the Active Directory (LDAP) is already configured, you will see the Active Directory name at the bottom of the AD icon in the \"Add User\" view."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter11.rst:108
msgid "Add Active Directory Users where those users are from local area network."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter11.rst:113
msgid "ADDING ACTIVE DIRECTORY USERS"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter11.rst:116
msgid "After the Active Directory is configured, you can use the Add User wizard to import Active Directory users into |prodname|."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter11.rst:121
msgid "For best practice, you will only configure Active Directory via LDAP if the file server is also local in the same network as the Active Directory server."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter11.rst:126
msgid "Active Directory Users from Server Agent"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter11.rst:128
msgid "When the Server Agent is available and connects to the specific tenant in |prodname|, the Server Agent will show up with the server's name at the bottom of the icon."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter11.rst:132
msgid "Click through the Server Agent icon, you will see the \"Add User\" wizard and complete the wizard to add users. This is very similar to the add AD user from local LDAP process above."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter11.rst:136
msgid "When the Active Directory is at a remote location, not directly connected to |prodname| server, Server Agent can be used to facilitate the communication. Server Agent doesn't need to be installed directly on a remote Active Directory server, the Server Agent needs to be installed on a remote file server that is part of the remote Active Directory domain."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter11.rst:140
msgid "Deleting Users"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter11.rst:142
msgid "When a user leaves the team, administrators can delete the user's login. Just click the Delete icon in 'User Manager' window."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter11.rst:147
msgid "DELETING A USER"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter11.rst:151
msgid "Managing User Quotas"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter11.rst:153
msgid "Administrators can assign a quota to each user. A user will not be allowed to upload files to |prodname| once their quota has been reached."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter11.rst:155
msgid "If the quota is 0 for the user, there is no limit on how much storage the user can use."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter11.rst:157
msgid "Click the 'Management Console' and select 'Users'. Click the \"Edit\" icon on an user to manage. On \"Storage\" tab, select \"Edit\" icon for storage quota."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter11.rst:162
msgid "EDITING STORAGE QUOTA"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter11.rst:166
msgid "Managing User Credentials"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter11.rst:168
msgid "Admins can change user passwords and login emails, if needed."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter11.rst:170
msgid "Click 'Management Console' and select 'User Manager'"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter11.rst:171
msgid "Click the \"manage user\" menu icon in the user block"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter11.rst:172
msgid "After that, can use \"Reset Password\" link to help the user."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter11.rst:177
msgid "RESET USER PASSWORD"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter11.rst:180
msgid "After changing the login password, an email will be sent to notify the user of the change. Admins can choose to include the new password in the email, or exclude the new password from the email. If the password is not included, the admin will need to convey the new password to the user in some other way."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter11.rst:185
msgid "PASSWORD OPTIONS"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter11.rst:188
msgid "When either the email or password is changed, please update the corresponding login credentials in the |prodname| Cloud Desktop or Cloud Server."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter11.rst:192
msgid "This only applies to a native |prodname| user. If you have Active Directory users, you will need to manage user's credential the Active Directory way."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter11.rst:196
msgid "Team Folders"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter11.rst:198
msgid "Adding files and folders can be accomplished by clicking \"Add a new team folder\" (**+**) icon on \"Team Folders\" page. Once the **\"Team Folder Storage Locations\"** view opens you can choose from many options: Existing Tenant Storage, File Servers in Local Area Network, Remote File Servers or Cloud Storage."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter11.rst:203
msgid "WAYS TO ADD STORAGE LOCATIONS"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter11.rst:206
msgid "**File Servers**"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter11.rst:208
msgid "If you have an existing file server in the Local Area Network (LAN), you can import the network share directly to |prodname| **(1)**. Under Remote File Servers, you can install the Server Agent client **(2)** and access your file server remotely."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter11.rst:213
msgid "ADDING REMOTE FILES"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter11.rst:218
msgid "The Server Agent is only required when the remote file server doesn't have direct LAN (local area network) access"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter11.rst:218
msgid "to |prodname|. The Server Agent will be used in this case to facilitate communication between the |prodname| server to the remote file server."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter11.rst:221
msgid "|prodname| enables the creation of team folders which are owned by the administrator and published to other |prodname| users."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter11.rst:223
msgid "Once a folder is published, it is displayed as a team folder to the users who have access permissions. Users can access these folders from |prodname| Web or other client agents. The published folder will appear under the user's root folder, and its name will be appended with \"(Team Folder)\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter11.rst:229
msgid "TEAM FOLDER TAG"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter11.rst:233
msgid "Different upload methods may have different advantage and disadvantage on different web browsers and different web browser configuration, such as whether it is HTML5 enabled, Java enabled or Flash enabled."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter11.rst:236
msgid "By default, only one upload method was exposed in the web user interface. However, the tenant administrator, based on the kind of web browser the company is using and the kind of configuration the web browser has, can decide which upload method to expose to the end user (Team User)."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter11.rst:239
msgid "Below is the Settings -> Clients & Applications -> Web Portal setting administrator can control."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter11.rst:244
msgid "UPLOADER METHOD OPTIONS"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter11.rst:246
msgid "Web Browser - Disable Java Uploader"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter11.rst:248
msgid "Deselect this if your companies' desktop system web browsers use a Java Uploader."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter11.rst:250
msgid "Web Browser - Disable Flash Uploader"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter11.rst:252
msgid "Deselect this if your company uses browsers that require Flash uploader functionality."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter11.rst:254
msgid "Web Browser - Disable Local Uploader"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter11.rst:256
msgid "Deselect this if your company allows the use of a local executable to upload files."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter11.rst:260
msgid "Sharing Security"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter11.rst:263
msgid "Preventing Users From Sharing"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter11.rst:265
msgid "Sometimes for security reasons, users should not be allowed to share files/folders."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter11.rst:267
msgid "There are two types of files and folders a user can access."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter11.rst:269
msgid "User's own folders, including versioned folders and attached local folders from the user's desktop."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter11.rst:271
msgid "When an administrator creates new users, he/she can disable sharing home directory content with external party, to prevent the newly created user from sharing his/her own files and folders."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter11.rst:277
msgid "MANAGE USER SETTINGS"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter11.rst:279
msgid "In the Manage User panel, access the \"Storage\" settings (4). Once you are in the Storage View you can select (5) the \"Disable external sharing of this user's home directory content\" option."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter11.rst:284
msgid "DISABLE EXTERNAL SHARING"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter11.rst:287
msgid "When publishing a team folder, administrator can check 'Disable further sharing', to prevent users from sharing anything in the team folder. You can access this setting after choosing your storage location. Click the \"Create Team Folder\" **(+)** icon (1) and select your storage type (2), \"New Team Folder\" window opens, click \"Settings\" icon (3), then select the \"Disable further sharing\" option (4)."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter11.rst:292
msgid "DISABLE FURTHER SHARING"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter11.rst:296
msgid "Protecting Shares By Requiring Login"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter11.rst:298
msgid "When a user shares a file or folder, |prodname| will generate a URL. By default, anyone can use the URL to access the share."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter11.rst:300
msgid "Administrators can protect shares by requiring login credentials. Once enabled, when a user accesses the share URL, he /she will be prompted to login to the |prodname| Cloud. After login, the user can view the file/folder shared with him/her under 'Files shared with me'."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter11.rst:303
msgid "To access this setting use the \"Settings\" menu (1) and in the \"Data Leak Protection\" (2) -> \"Sharing\" (3) panel, select the \"Users must log in to access the content in 'Files shared with me' folder\" setting (4)."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter11.rst:308
msgid "SECURING SHARED FILES AND FOLDERS"
msgstr ""
